From: Bellatrix Project <bellatrix@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] vc4gallium: normalize indexed primitive fields

Mesa writes the count, index-buffer offset, and maximum index of its manually
assembled GL_INDEXED_PRIMITIVE packet with cl_u32, which is host-endian.  Read
all three safely in host order and emit them little-endian for V3D while
relocating the buffer address.  Previously emu68 completed black frames after
using a byte-swapped index offset and forwarding byte-swapped draw bounds.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vc4gallium/vc4_drm_aros.c b/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vc4gallium/vc4_drm_aros.c
--- a/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vc4gallium/vc4_drm_aros.c
+++ b/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vc4gallium/vc4_drm_aros.c
@@ -1548,9 +1548,15 @@ static ULONG process_bin_cl(struct exec_state *exec,
             if (dst_off + pkt_size > dst_max) return 0;
             CopyMem(src + src_off, dst + dst_off, pkt_size);
 
-            /* Patch index buffer address: offset is at byte 6 (after cmd+mode+count) */
-            ULONG ib_offset = get_u32_unaligned(src + src_off + 6);
+            /* Mesa emits these manual cl_u32 fields in host order. Convert
+             * all three to the little-endian representation consumed by
+             * V3D, relocating the index-buffer offset along the way. */
+            ULONG count = get_u32_native_unaligned(src + src_off + 2);
+            ULONG ib_offset = get_u32_native_unaligned(src + src_off + 6);
+            ULONG max_index = get_u32_native_unaligned(src + src_off + 10);
+            put_u32_unaligned(dst + dst_off + 2, count);
             put_u32_unaligned(dst + dst_off + 6, exec->current_bo[0] + ib_offset);
+            put_u32_unaligned(dst + dst_off + 10, max_index);
 
             dst_off += pkt_size;
             src_off += pkt_size;
-- 
